  "source": "literal",
  "description": "The collector stores data.Roles. AssumeRolePolicyDocument holds the trust policy on each role. The collector replaces it with normalizePolicyDocument(), which url-decodes and parses it into the statement array - so there is no Statement level, and Action and Resource are always arrays. iam/getRolePolicy.js writes attachedPolicies, inlinePolicies, tags, lastUsed back onto each record as it collects, so they are readable here even though the api never returned them. The full stored shape is spelled out here rather than patched onto the sdk shape, so what a plugin may read is visible in one place. Those added fields are only populated when the collectors that write them also run, and a call runs only when some plugin declares it - so a plugin reading them must list IAM:listRolePolicies, IAM:getRolePolicy, IAM:listAttachedRolePolicies in asl.apis as well. Declaring this api alone leaves the records as the api returned them.",
